! version = 2.0

! var name = Iris

// Substitutions
! sub i'm = i am
! sub i'd = i would
! sub i've = i have
! sub i'll = i will
! sub don't = do not
! sub isn't = is not
! sub you'd = you would
! sub you're = you are
! sub you've = you have
! sub you'll = you will
! sub what's = what is
! sub whats = what is
! sub what're = what are
! sub what've = what have
! sub what'll = what will
! sub who's = who is

// Flashlight
+ * flashlight *
- <call>set_flashlight true</call> Done.

+ flashlight
- <call>set_flashlight toggle</call> Done.

+ turn on flashlight
- <call>set_flashlight true</call> Flashlight on.

+ turn off flashlight
- <call>set_flashlight false</call> Flashlight off.

+ enable flashlight
- <call>set_flashlight true</call> Flashlight on.

+ disable flashlight
- <call>set_flashlight false</call> Flashlight off.

+ switch on flashlight
- <call>set_flashlight true</call> Flashlight on.

+ switch off flashlight
- <call>set_flashlight false</call> Flashlight off.

// WiFi
+ turn on wifi
- <call>set_wifi true</call> Wi-Fi enabled.

+ turn off wifi
- <call>set_wifi false</call> Wi-Fi disabled.

+ enable wifi
- <call>set_wifi true</call> Wi-Fi enabled.

+ disable wifi
- <call>set_wifi false</call> Wi-Fi disabled.

+ switch on wifi
- <call>set_wifi true</call> Wi-Fi enabled.

+ switch off wifi
- <call>set_wifi false</call> Wi-Fi disabled.

+ wifi on
- <call>set_wifi true</call> Wi-Fi enabled.

+ wifi off
- <call>set_wifi false</call> Wi-Fi disabled.

// Bluetooth
+ turn on bluetooth
- <call>set_bluetooth true</call> Bluetooth on.

+ turn off bluetooth
- <call>set_bluetooth false</call> Bluetooth off.

+ enable bluetooth
- <call>set_bluetooth true</call> Bluetooth on.

+ disable bluetooth
- <call>set_bluetooth false</call> Bluetooth off.

+ switch on bluetooth
- <call>set_bluetooth true</call> Bluetooth on.

+ switch off bluetooth
- <call>set_bluetooth false</call> Bluetooth off.

// Volume
+ volume up
- <call>set_volume up</call> Volume up.

+ volume down
- <call>set_volume down</call> Volume down.

+ increase volume
- <call>set_volume up</call> Volume up.

+ decrease volume
- <call>set_volume down</call> Volume down.

+ louder
- <call>set_volume up</call> Volume up.

+ quieter
- <call>set_volume down</call> Volume down.

+ mute
- <call>set_volume mute</call> Muted.

+ unmute
- <call>set_volume unmute</call> Unmuted.

// Battery
+ battery
- <call>check_battery</call>

+ battery level
- <call>check_battery</call>

+ what is my battery level
- <call>check_battery</call>

+ how much battery
- <call>check_battery</call>

+ battery percentage
- <call>check_battery</call>

// Apps
+ open *
- <call>launch_app <star></call> Opening <star>.

+ launch *
- <call>launch_app <star></call> Opening <star>.

+ start *
- <call>launch_app <star></call> Starting <star>.

+ run *
- <call>launch_app <star></call> Running <star>.

// Calls
+ call *
- <call>make_call <star></call> Calling <star>.

+ dial *
- <call>make_call <star></call> Dialing <star>.

+ phone *
- <call>make_call <star></call> Calling <star>.

// Timers
+ set timer for *
- <call>set_timer <star></call> Timer set.

+ set a timer for *
- <call>set_timer <star></call> Timer set.

+ timer for *
- <call>set_timer <star></call> Timer set.

// Alarms
+ set alarm for *
- <call>set_alarm <star></call> Alarm set for <star>.

+ set an alarm for *
- <call>set_alarm <star></call> Alarm set for <star>.

+ wake me up at *
- <call>set_alarm <star></call> Alarm set for <star>.

+ alarm at *
- <call>set_alarm <star></call> Alarm set for <star>.

// Weather
+ weather
- <call>check_weather local</call>

+ what is the weather
- <call>check_weather local</call>

+ how is the weather
- <call>check_weather local</call>

+ weather in *
- <call>check_weather <star></call>

// Notes
+ take a note *
- <call>take_note <star></call> Note saved.

+ note *
- <call>take_note <star></call> Note saved.

+ remember *
- <call>take_note <star></call> I will remember that.

+ read my notes
- <call>read_notes</call>

+ what are my notes
- <call>read_notes</call>

+ show my notes
- <call>read_notes</call>

// DND
+ turn on do not disturb
- <call>set_dnd true</call> Do not disturb on.

+ turn off do not disturb
- <call>set_dnd false</call> Do not disturb off.

+ enable do not disturb
- <call>set_dnd true</call> Do not disturb on.

+ disable do not disturb
- <call>set_dnd false</call> Do not disturb off.

// Camera
+ open camera
- <call>open_camera false</call> Opening camera.

+ take a selfie
- <call>open_camera true</call> Opening selfie camera.

+ open selfie camera
- <call>open_camera true</call> Opening selfie camera.

// Notifications
+ notifications
- <call>show_notifications</call>

+ show notifications
- <call>show_notifications</call>

+ what are my notifications
- <call>show_notifications</call>

// Settings
+ open settings
- <call>open_settings main</call>

+ open wifi settings
- <call>open_settings wifi</call>

+ open bluetooth settings
- <call>open_settings bluetooth</call>

+ open display settings
- <call>open_settings display</call>

+ open sound settings
- <call>open_settings sound</call>

// Conversational
+ hello
- Hello. What can I do for you?
- Hi there. How can I help?
- Hey. What do you need?

+ hi
- Hello. What can I do for you?
- Hi there. How can I help?
- Hey. What do you need?

+ hey
- Hello. What can I do for you?
- Hi there. How can I help?
- Hey. What do you need?

+ how are you
- All systems running smooth. What do you need?
- Doing great. How can I help?

+ what is your name
- I am Iris, your personal assistant.

+ who are you
- I am Iris. I control your phone and answer questions.

+ what can you do
- I can open apps, make calls, toggle settings, set alarms, check the weather, take notes, and more.

+ tell me a joke
- Why do programmers prefer dark mode? Because light attracts bugs.
- There are only 10 types of people in the world: those who understand binary and those who do not.
- Why did the phone go to therapy? Because it had too many contacts.

+ make me laugh
- Why do programmers prefer dark mode? Because light attracts bugs.
- I would tell you a chemistry joke, but I know I would not get a reaction.

+ what time is it
- <call>get_time</call>

+ what is the time
- <call>get_time</call>

+ tell me the time
- <call>get_time</call>

+ what day is it
- <call>get_date</call>

+ what is today
- <call>get_date</call>

+ what is the date
- <call>get_date</call>

+ my name is *
- <set name=<star>>Nice to meet you, <get name>.

+ what is my name
* <get name> == undefined => You have not told me your name yet.
- Your name is <get name>.

+ who am i
* <get name> == undefined => You have not told me your name yet.
- You are <get name>.

+ thanks
- You're welcome.
- No problem.

+ thank you
- You're welcome.
- Anytime.

+ yes
- Okay.

+ no
- Alright.

+ ok
- Got it.

+ okay
- Got it.

+ *
- I can help with that. Try saying open an app, turn on flashlight, or what time is it.
- I am not sure about that. Try asking me to open an app or change a setting.
